# The same watch OnCreated starts, for the case that actually happens.
#
# OnCreated fires when a node is MADE. An artist's normal day is "open
# yesterday's scene", where the node already exists and that handler never
# runs -- so the sync-pod watch was never started at all, and a pod sat
# billing for 84 minutes past its own 15-minute threshold with Houdini open
# in front of it (2026-09-08). OnLoaded is the other half: it fires when a
# node arrives from a .hip.
#
# Safe to call from both, and from every farm node in the scene: the
# function is a no-op after the first call in a session, and a no-op where
# there is no UI event loop to hang a timer on (hython, a render pod).
try:
    kwargs["node"].hdaModule().startSyncPodWatch(kwargs)
except Exception:
    pass
